# Knowledge harness

This repo (`sam-dev-site/leif-in-the-wind`) is the source of truth. Chat memory is not.

Before project work, read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/MISSION.md`, `docs/DECISIONS.md`, and `docs/STATUS.md`.

If you make a lasting decision, append `docs/DECISIONS.md` in the same session. Update `docs/STATUS.md` before you finish.

When the owner signs off (`commit`, `save`, `all set`, `good`, `done`, `push`), run git in that turn. Do not ask, and do not report a hash git did not print. `push` also pushes. See `.cursor/rules/commit-signoff.mdc`.

Bugs that are not the current Play live in `docs/BUGS.md`. Log them there and leave them. When the owner asks to do bug fixes, read that file and name the open headings before changing the game. New wishes stay in `docs/IDEAS.md`.

Never invent biome species. If it is not in `docs/research/biomes/`, research it with sources first.

Prefer cloud agent + PR over loading this Surface Pro. Local machine is for playtest.

Slice docs do not override `docs/MISSION.md`. Features serve the named aesthetics (sensation, fantasy, discovery, submission), not only inland movement.
